---
// Money page. Copy authored by content-writer against briefs/home.json (2026-07-13).
// Experience claims trace to config/expertise-library.md; regulatory facts to the
// CANONICAL block in config/business-context.md (HDB rule 62 verified on hdb.gov.sg).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import AnswerCapsule from '../components/AnswerCapsule.astro';
import StatStrip from '../components/StatStrip.astro';
import ListingGrid from '../components/ListingGrid.astro';
import CaptionedBlock from '../components/CaptionedBlock.astro';
import FactsCard from '../components/FactsCard.astro';
import CloudDivider from '../components/CloudDivider.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CtaClose from '../components/CtaClose.astro';
import { site, whatsappLink } from '../data/site';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema, productSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { availablePups } from '../data/puppies';

const title = 'Maltipoo Singapore | Toy Maltipoo Puppies | Maltipoo.sg';
const description =
  'Toy Maltipoo puppies in Singapore from $3,288 all-in, by AVS licensed Curious Tails (AS24J00046). Starter kit, delivery, first training lesson and licensing included. WhatsApp us.';

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'How much does a Maltipoo cost in Singapore?',
    a: 'Maltipoo puppies at Maltipoo.sg are $3,288 to $5,988 all-in, depending on colour and adult size. That covers the 30-item starter kit, home delivery with playpen setup, the first training lesson, and the AVS licensing paperwork done at purchase. Around the market you will see anything from promo listings to five-figure imports, usually before extras.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are Maltipoos HDB approved?',
    a: 'Yes, by rule. HDB’s approved list names the Maltese at item 33 and the Toy and Miniature Poodle at item 42, and item 62 approves a cross of any two approved breeds, which is exactly what a Maltipoo is. Across 100+ placements, our licence transfers to HDB homes have never been flagged either.',
  },
  {
    q: 'When can my Maltipoo puppy come home?',
    a: 'Around week nine, about a week after the second vaccination. Core jabs run at weeks 6, 8 and 12 with deworming at each visit, and an optional fourth jab at week 16 if your vet advises it. If your home is not ready yet, we board your puppy free for up to a month after deposit.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can a Maltipoo be left alone while we are at work?',
    a: 'Honestly, this is not the breed for an empty weekday home. Maltipoos are attachment-dependent and want daytime company. They thrive with retirees, WFH owners, and households with a helper or grandparent at home. If everyone is out 8am to 6pm, a Cavapoo suits that routine better, and we will say so.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How big does a toy Maltipoo get?',
    a: 'The Maltipoos we place are toy-sized, finishing around 2 to 4kg full grown. That featherweight build is part of the appeal: lap-sized on the sofa, carrier-friendly on the MRT, and comfortable in any flat.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much is the dog licence, and when is it due?',
    a: 'The AVS dog licence for your first year costs $13.50, because puppies go home at around nine weeks, under the five-month threshold. From five months an unsterilised dog is $81 a year; once sterilised it drops to $13.50 a year or a one-time $35 lifetime licence. We complete the paperwork with you at purchase.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I check a pet shop is AVS licensed?',
    a: 'Look the shop up on the AVS public registry of licensed pet shops on the NParks site. Curious Tails, the shop behind Maltipoo.sg, holds AVS licence AS24J00046. Verify it there before visiting us or anyone else.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do Maltipoos shed?',
    a: 'Maltipoos are low-shedding, not non-shedding. The Poodle side keeps loose hair in the coat rather than on your sofa, which is also why regular brushing and grooming matter. No dog is truly hypoallergenic, so allergy-sensitive buyers should meet the puppy in person first.',
  },
];

const schemas = [
  webPageSchema({
    path: '/',
    title,
    description,
    aboutName: 'Maltipoo puppies in Singapore',
    datePublished: '2026-07-13',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }]),
  productSchema({
    name: 'Maltipoo puppy (Singapore)',
    description: 'Toy Maltipoo puppies from an AVS licensed pet shop in Singapore, $3,288 to $5,988 all-in.',
  }),
  faqSchema(faqItems),
];

const coatSwatches = [
  ['Cream apricot', '#f4e3c8'],
  ['Apricot', '#e8b985'],
  ['Deep apricot', '#d19158'],
  ['Apricot & white', '#f7efe2'],
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/" schemas={schemas}>
  <Hero
    heading="Maltipoo puppies in Singapore, matched to homes with company"
    lede="Toy Maltipoos, 2 to 4kg full grown, from the AVS licensed shop that asks about your routine before showing you a puppy. Every Maltipoo goes home vaccinated on the 6, 8 and 12 week schedule, licensed at purchase, and set up with the full 30-item starter kit. From $3,288, all-in."
    ctaMessage="Hi! I would like to ask about Maltipoo puppies."
    secondaryLabel="See available puppies"
    secondaryHref="#recent"
  />

  <section class="container-site pt-2">
    <p class="text-ink-soft max-w-[65ch] m-0">
      Every "Maltipoo for sale Singapore" page you have open probably shows different puppies
      by now; availability moves week to week. WhatsApp us to confirm a puppy, then book a
      viewing at the Balestier shop.
    </p>
  </section>
  <ListingGrid heading="Maltipoo puppies for sale in Singapore" items={availablePups} mode="available" id="recent" />

  <AnswerCapsule question="What is a Maltipoo?" id="what-is-a-maltipoo">
    A Maltipoo is a small companion cross between a Maltese and a Toy or Miniature Poodle,
    often described as a Maltese Poodle mix, typically 2 to 4kg full grown in the toy sizes we
    place, with a soft low-shedding coat that in Singapore is most often apricot. It pairs the Maltese devotion to its people with the
    Poodle's quick mind, which makes it a devoted lap dog for homes where someone is usually
    around.
  </AnswerCapsule>

  <StatStrip
    stats={[
      { value: site.maltipoosPlaced, label: 'Maltipoos placed in Singapore' },
      { value: site.reviews.rating, label: `Google rating (${site.reviews.count} reviews)` },
      { value: site.pricing.from, label: 'All-in, nothing hidden' },
      { value: 'AVS', label: `Licence ${site.license.avsNumber}` },
    ]}
  />

  <CaptionedBlock heading="A velcro dog, and proud of it" id="why-maltipoo">
    <p>
      Some breeds tolerate your company. A Maltipoo insists on it: it follows you from room to
      room, naps against your leg, and treats your lap as assigned seating. For the right home,
      that devotion is exactly the point, not a flaw to be managed.
    </p>
    <p>
      After 100+ placements we can tell you precisely who the right home is: retirees, people
      who work from home, and families with a helper or a grandparent around through the day.
      That is the toy Maltipoo Singapore homes keep coming back for, and those placements are
      the ones we keep hearing from.
      <!-- TODO: link /maltipoo-temperament once built -->
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Maltipoo at a glance"
      items={[
        'Maltese × Toy or Miniature Poodle cross',
        'Toy-sized: 2 to 4kg for most of ours',
        'Low-shedding coat, apricot most common here',
        'Deeply people-attached; wants daytime company',
        'Featherweight and carrier-friendly',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CloudDivider fill="var(--color-tint-200)" against="var(--color-base)" />
  <div style="background: var(--color-tint-200);">
    <CaptionedBlock heading="The one question we ask before showing you a puppy" id="lifestyle-fit">
      <p>
        Who is home between 8am and 6pm? At the shop we ask it before colour, before size,
        before budget, because it is the single number that decides whether a Maltipoo
        placement works.
      </p>
      <p>
        If someone is around most of the day, a Maltipoo will be the happiest dog in the block.
        If the flat empties out every weekday, we will say so plainly and point you to a more
        independent breed; our sister shop places Cavapoos for exactly that routine.
        <!-- TODO: link /maltipoo-vs-cavapoo once built -->
      </p>
      <p>
        A note from the shop floor: talking a buyer out of the wrong dog costs us a sale that
        week and earns us a referral the next. We have made that trade many times, and it is
        why our reviews mention honest advice more than anything else.
      </p>
      <FactsCard
        slot="side"
        heading="Which routine are you?"
        items={[
          'Someone home most of the day: the Maltipoo sweet spot',
          'WFH with meetings: yes, with a settled pen routine',
          'Both out 8am to 6pm daily: consider a Cavapoo instead',
          'Away morning to night: we will advise against a puppy for now',
        ]}
      />
    </CaptionedBlock>
  </div>
  <CloudDivider fill="var(--color-tint-200)" against="var(--color-base)" flip />

  <CaptionedBlock heading="What every Maltipoo goes home with" id="included" reverse>
    <p>
      All-in means an itemised list, not a slogan. The starter kit runs to 30 items worth over
      $500: playpen, carrier, bed, grooming set, toilet-training set, food, bowls, oral care
      and toys. We deliver it free, assemble the playpen in your home, and walk you through how
      every item works before we leave.
    </p>
    <p>
      The first lesson with an AVS-certified trainer is included, and the dog licence paperwork
      is completed with you at purchase, so nothing is left hanging after handover.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Included with every puppy"
      items={[
        'Starter kit: 30 items, over $500 in value',
        'Free home delivery and playpen setup',
        'First lesson with an AVS-certified trainer',
        'AVS licensing completed at purchase',
        'Free boarding up to 1 month after deposit',
        '5-day bring-back care if your puppy falls sick',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <section class="container-site py-10" id="price">
    <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-panel)] bg-tint-200 p-8 md:p-12 grid md:grid-cols-[1.4fr_1fr] gap-8 items-center">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Transparent pricing</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">Maltipoo price in Singapore: {site.pricing.fromLine}</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-soft mb-4 max-w-[60ch]">
          Our all-in price for a Maltipoo puppy is {site.pricing.range}; colour and adult size
          decide where a puppy sits in that range. Deposit, then balance, and nothing added at
          collection. Scroll the "Maltipoo price Singapore" results and you will find
          everything from $2,000-plus promo listings to imported puppies quoted near five
          figures, usually before extras, and most sellers publish no prices at all. We would
          rather you compare with real numbers in front of you. The full
          <a href="/maltipoo-price-singapore">price guide</a> breaks down what moves a puppy
          within the range.
          <!-- TODO: link /blog/maltipoo-cost-ownership once built -->
        </p>
        <a href={whatsappLink('Hi! Could you share current Maltipoo pricing and availability?')} class="btn-cta">Ask about pricing</a>
      </div>
      <div class="pop p-6">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-soft m-0 mb-1">Maltipoo puppies</p>
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary m-0 mb-3" style="font-family: var(--font-display);">{site.pricing.range}</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft m-0">
          all-in, including the starter kit, delivery and setup, first training lesson, and
          licensing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <AnswerCapsule question="Is a Maltipoo HDB approved?" id="hdb">
    Yes, and not just in practice: HDB's
    <a href="https://www.hdb.gov.sg/managing-my-home/home-ownership/keeping-pets" rel="noopener" target="_blank">approved breeds list</a>
    names the Maltese at item 33 and the Toy and Miniature Poodle at item 42, and item 62
    approves a cross of any two approved breeds. A Maltipoo qualifies by rule, which makes the
    HDB approved Maltipoo a settled question rather than a grey area. Our licence transfers to
    HDB homes, across {site.maltipoosPlaced} placements, have never been flagged either. One
    dog per flat, AVS licence required. The
    <a href="/maltipoo-hdb-approved">full HDB guide</a> walks through the proof and the rules.
  </AnswerCapsule>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="From our shop to your sofa: the week-by-week timeline" id="timeline">
    <p>
      The puppy vaccination schedule Singapore vets follow runs core jabs at weeks 6, 8 and 12,
      with deworming at every visit and an optional fourth jab at week 16 if the vet advises it. Your puppy goes home about a week after the
      second jab, at around week nine, and the annual booster starts from Year 1.
    </p>
    <p>
      Renovating, travelling, or waiting for the flat to be ready? After a deposit we board
      your puppy free for up to one month, vaccinations continuing on schedule at our cost, and
      deliver when you are ready.
    </p>
    <p>
      A first time dog owner in Singapore also needs one extra step: the
      <a href="https://avs.nparks.gov.sg/pets/licensing-a-pet/applying-for-dog-and-cat-licences/pet-ownership-course/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">AVS Pet Ownership Course</a>
      before the first licence; we point you to it during purchase so paperwork never delays
      the homecoming.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="The timeline"
      items={[
        'Week 6: first vaccination + deworming',
        'Week 8: second vaccination + deworming',
        'Week 9: puppy goes home (about a week after the 2nd jab)',
        'Week 12: third vaccination + deworming',
        'Week 16: optional 4th jab if the vet advises',
        'Year 1 onward: annual booster',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <section class="container-site py-10" id="colours">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Coats and colours</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">Apricot, mostly: what we actually place</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft max-w-[65ch] mb-6">
      Maltipoos come in white, cream, apricot and the occasional black, but what comes through
      our shop is overwhelmingly apricot, so an apricot Maltipoo for sale here is the norm
      rather than the exception, from pale cream-apricot to deep amber. Puppy coats
      usually lighten as they mature, so we show you the parents' colouring in person rather
      than promise a shade from a photo.
      <!-- TODO: link /maltipoo-colours and /maltipoo-size once built -->
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
      {coatSwatches.map(([name, hex]) => (
        <div class="pop p-4 text-center">
          <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-media)] w-full aspect-square mb-3" style={`background:${hex}`} aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="font-semibold m-0">{name}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Daily life with a 2 to 4kg dog in a Singapore flat" id="daily-life" reverse>
    <p>
      Plan the walk before the heat: fifteen to twenty minutes in the morning, then indoor play
      in the evening suits a toy Maltipoo fine. Feeding is three small meals a day for a young
      puppy, tapering to two, and the playpen from the kit anchors the daytime routine.
    </p>
    <p>
      The coat is the real commitment. In our humidity, a few brushes a week keeps matting off
      and a professional groom every four to six weeks keeps the teddy bear cut tidy. Maltipoo
      grooming Singapore salons quote about $50 to $70 for a basic groom on a toy-sized dog
      and $80 to $130 for a full one. The
      daily 60-second eye wipe is what keeps apricot faces stain-free; see the
      <a href="/blog/maltipoo-tear-stains">tear-stain routine</a> for the whole method.
      <!-- TODO: link /maltipoo-grooming-haircuts once built -->
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="A first-time owner's week"
      items={[
        'Morning: 15-minute walk before the heat',
        'Daytime: playpen routine with toys and water',
        'Evening: dinner, indoor play, lap time',
        'Few times weekly: brushing to stop matting',
        'Every 4 to 6 weeks: professional groom',
        'Daily: 60-second eye-corner wipe',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Buying safely: verify us, and anyone else, in 60 seconds" id="verify" tinted>
    <p>
      Every legitimate pet shop in Singapore is listed on the
      <a href="https://avs.nparks.gov.sg/outreach/resources/public-registry-of-avs-licensed-pet-shops/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">AVS public registry of licensed pet shops</a>.
      Curious Tails, the shop behind this site, holds licence {site.license.avsNumber}; check
      it before you visit, and check any other seller the same way.
    </p>
    <p>
      Searches like "where to buy Maltipoo in Singapore" and "Maltipoo puppies for sale
      Singapore under $500" surface everything from licensed shops to smuggled litters that
      never saw a vet, and NParks has fined a buyer $7,000 for the wrong choice. Any Maltipoo
      breeder Singapore buyers shortlist should appear on that registry; if it does not, walk
      away. Licensed shop, published pricing, paperwork at purchase: the boring route is the
      safe one, and we are happy to be boring.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Your 60-second check"
      items={[
        'Search the AVS registry for the shop name',
        'Match the licence number: ours is AS24J00046',
        'Visit the physical shop, ours is at Balestier',
        'Expect vaccination records for weeks 6 and 8',
        'Walk away from meet-in-carpark deals',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <section class="container-site py-10" id="reviews">
    <div class="pop p-8 md:p-10 grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-6 items-center">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-2">From a Maltipoo family</p>
        <blockquote class="m-0 text-lg text-ink leading-relaxed">
          "We'd been comparing breeders for weeks, and Curious Tails in Balestier stood head
          and shoulders above the rest. It was clear Nelson knew their stuff, as they were
          happy to help with even the small things and knew their stuff inside and out.
          Everything from the health records to the paperwork was handled seamlessly. The
          $500+ starter pack was such a generous surprise and got us set up right away. We
          couldn't be more pleased, an easy five stars."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft mt-3 mb-0">Karen Joy, Google review, after bringing home her Maltipoo</p>
      </div>
      <div class="text-center px-6">
        <p class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary m-0" style="font-family: var(--font-display);">{site.reviews.rating}</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft m-0">{site.reviews.count} Google reviews</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="After the sale: the part most shops skip" id="aftercare">
    <p>
      If your puppy falls sick in the first five days, bring it back to us and we handle the
      care. That bring-back promise sits alongside free boarding for up to a month after
      deposit, the included trainer lesson, and ongoing care advice for as long as you need it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of our WhatsApp threads stay active long after handover: food questions, grooming
      questions, the odd 10pm photo of a puppy asleep in the wrong bed. That is the part of the
      job we like best, and the reason families come back for their second dog.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Aftercare, in writing"
      items={[
        '5-day bring-back care if your puppy falls sick',
        'Free boarding up to 1 month after deposit',
        'First training lesson with an AVS-certified trainer',
        'Free ongoing care advice, no expiry',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />

  <section class="container-site pb-4">
    <p class="text-ink-soft max-w-[65ch] m-0">
      Checking Maltipoo adoption Singapore shelters first is a fine instinct; rescues rarely
      have toy crosses, but look before you buy. Most Maltipoo SG searches end at a listing
      page; ours ends at a real shop you can walk into. Every Maltipoo puppy Singapore families take home from us starts at 2 Balestier
      Road #01-701, a short walk from Novena MRT, with paid parking behind the block. Weekdays
      12pm to 6pm, weekends 10am to 6pm, viewings by appointment. Come on a weekend morning,
      meet the puppies, and take your time; honest advice costs nothing here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <CtaClose
    secondaryHeading="Still deciding?"
    secondaryText="Start with the pricing panel above: every dollar explained, no surprises at the shop."
    secondaryHref="#price"
    secondaryLabel="Review the pricing"
  />
</BaseLayout>
